   "": {
    "actClause": "AN ACT to amend the environmental conservation law, in relation to extending\nthe authority of the department of environmental conservation to restrict the\ntaking of fish, shellfish and crustacea in special management areas",
    "basePrintNo": "S6949",
    "basePrintNoStr": "S6949-2023",
    "coSponsors": {
     "items": [],
     "size": 0
    },
    "fullText": "",
    "fullTextFormats": [],
    "fullTextHtml": "",
    "fullTextTemplate": "",
    "lawCode": "Amd §13-0360, En Con L",
    "lawSection": "Environmental Conservation Law",
    "memo": " \nBILL NUMBER: S6949\n\nSPONSOR: FERNANDEZ\n \nTITLE OF BILL:\n\nAn act to amend the environmental conservation law, in relation to\nextending the authority of the department of environmental conservation\nto restrict the taking of fish, shellfish and crustacea in special\nmanagement areas\n\n \nPURPOSE OF THE BILL:\n\nThe purpose of this bill is to extend the authority of the Department of\nEnvironmental Conservation (DEC) to adopt regulations restricting the\ntaking of fish, shellfish, and crustacea in Special Management Areas.\n\n \nSUMMARY OF PROVISIONS:\n\nSection 1 of this bill amends Environmental Conservation Law (ECL) §\n13-0360(3) to extend, until December 31, 2026, DEC's authority to adopt\nregulations restricting the taking of fish, shellfish, and crustacea in\nany designated Special Management Area.\n\nSection 2 of this bill provides that the bill shall take effect imme-\ndiately.\n\n \nJUSTIFICATION:\n\nProtection of the State's valuable reef ecosystems is an integral part\nof the overall management of the marine resources of the marine and\ncoastal district. As defined in law, these Special Management Areas are\ncomposed of artificial reefs as well as shipwrecks which provide habitat\nand safe havens for fish, shellfish and crustacea. DEC's authority to\nadopt regulations restricting the taking of fish, shellfish and crusta-\ncea in these areas must be extended by December 31, 2023 to assure the\ncontinuation of protective measures for reef fisheries.\n\n \nPRIOR LEGISLATIVE HISTORY:\n\nLast extended by Chapter 58 of the Laws of 2020.\n\n \nFISCAL IMPLICATIONS:\n\nNone.\n\n \nEFFECTIVE DATE:\nThis act shall take effect immediately.\n",
